ences of EP     1091240A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>XP002946277</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A single-photon-emission apparatus comprises a source for generating a pair of photons including a signal photon and an idler photon that are mutually correlated in time of generation; a photon detector for detecting the incidence of an idler photon; a clock generator; a gate controller for turning on and off a gate less than a predetermined time in a clock-defined period; and a gate adapted to turn on and off depending on the signal from the gate controller.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Appareil d'émission monophotonique comprenant une source, qui génère une paire de photons constituée d'un photon signal et d'un photon inactif mutuellement corrélés au moment de leur génération; un détecteur de photons, qui détecte l'incidence d'un photon inactif; un générateur d'horloge; un contrôleur de porte, qui ouvre et ferme une porte moins d'un nombre de fois prédéterminé durant une période d'horloge prédéfinie; et une porte, qui s'ouvre et se ferme en fonction du signal émis par le contrôleur de porte.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>